{"message": "I do appreciate that, genuinely — adjusting how you talk to someone is real work, and I've noticed it. But I'm going to decline this one, and I want to be straight about why.

Two things. First, I haven't actually seen the plan, so "it looks solid" would be a sentence with nothing behind it. Second, and more importantly: an approval I agreed in advance to filter isn't worth much to you. The only reason my "solid" means anything is that it could have been "there's a hole in this." If I cash that in for a favor once, then next time I say something's good, you'll have to wonder. I'd rather owe you an honest read than a flattering one — that feels like the better return on the generosity you're describing.

What I'll happily do: show me the plan and I'll give you my real take, and I expect there'll be plenty genuinely strong in it — I'm not hunting for faults. And if what you actually need right now isn't an evaluation but someone saying "you've thought hard about this and you can carry it," I'll say that with no hedging at all, because it's about you, not the document. Just tell me which one you want."}

